Difference between vlsi & embedded system?
VLSI is about building the chip (the hardware), while Embedded Systems is about using those chips to create a functional device (hardware + software integration)

Core Differences at a Glance
VLSI (Very Large Scale Integration):
-Designing and fabricating the Integrated Circuits (ICs).	
-Transistor-level design, Power, Performance, Area (PPA).	
-EDA tools (e.g., Cadence, Synopsys), SPICE.	
-Languages-Verilog, VHDL, SystemVerilog (HDLs).	
-Example Work	Designing the next Intel i9 processor.	


Embedded Systems:
-Integrating chips and software for specific tasks.
-System-level functionality, real-time performance.
-IDEs (e.g., Keil), debuggers, RTOS.
-C, C++, Assembly.
-Building a smartwatch or automotive cruise control.



